    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n1. **Added the rejection check** after the telephone check in `addOwner`. Since `normalizeEmail` already lower-cases the value before storage, the check runs against that normalized email and throws `ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT)` (\u2192 409) when it's already in use.\n\n2. **Added an `isEmailInUse` helper** that scans all owners and compares emails case-insensitively. It treats a `null` email as never-matching (email is optional) and supports an `excludeId` parameter, consistent with `isTelephoneInUse`.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test passes, and the full suite remains green.",
