        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `isEmailInUse` is a faithful sibling of the existing `isTelephoneInUse` method it sits directly beside: same signature shape (`(value, excludeId)`), same loop-over-`findAllOwners()` structure, same `excludeId` skip logic, and a Javadoc written in the same style as its neighbors. The call site in `addOwner` slots in right after the telephone conflict check, mirroring it exactly (same 409 pattern, parallel message wording). The `null` email short-circuit is consistent with the \"email is optional\" convention established by `normalizeEmail`, and case-insensitive comparison matches the idiom used by `countOwnersInCity` / `countNamesakes`. Logic is in the right unit, nothing is duplicated, and the controller isn't becoming a catch-all beyond the sibling-validator pattern it already uses. A maintainer would find this natural."
